    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3c7c178b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: all_races_unite_against_islam; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two hands clasped together in a gesture of unity, juxtaposed with the text 'all races unite against islam!' This visual metaphor is used to promote division and hostility toward Muslims, framing them as an enemy to be opposed by all racial groups. The meme is explicitly hateful as it targets a specific religious group with a call to collective action against them, which is a direct attack on Muslims based on their religion. It promotes xenophobia and Islamophobia by encouraging unity against a religious minority, which can incite prejudice and violence. The use of the phrase 'all races unite' ironically contrasts with the divisive message, highlighting the meme's intent to weaponize solidarity for hateful purposes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e6c3c2a6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
